        "text": "Academic Programs Fast Track SHS SHS (NCIP) fast_track.html Search results Fast Track SHS Fast Track SHS Education with a global outlook Program Offering Flexible Learning Global Opportunities Academic Timeline Why Enroll at NCIP - IIIP? NCIP “Snap & Submit” Enrollment Paradigm PHASE 1: DISTRIBUTION PHASE 2: SNAP & SUBMIT PHASE 3: ENCODING & VERIFICATION PHASE 4: OFFICIAL ONBOARDING HUMSS Competency-Based Curriculum (CBC) Modules Empowering Indigenous Futures Globally Address Quick Links Gallery Contact Us Visit Us Fast Track SHS National Commission for Indigenous Peoples (NCIP)International Institute of Indigenous Peoples (IIIP) GLOBAL EDUCATION · DIGITAL SKILLS · INDIGENOUS EMPOWERMENT Fast Track SHS Powered by St. Robert's International College- Iloilo, PhilippinesSt. Robert's International College - Bangkok, Thailand Grade 11 (SY 2025 - 2026) Fast-Tracked: Jan 2026 to Jul 2026 | Modules 1 & 2 Explore Programs ↓ View brochure ↗ Program overview Academic timeline How to enroll HUMSS curriculum CBC modules YOUR LEARNING PATHWAY Education with a global outlook Program Offering Senior High School + Digital Engineering Modules (Grades 11 & 12) 2 Digital Engineering Modules per Grade Level 4 months per module ISO 17024 International Certification Flexible Learning 100% Online Classes Face-to-Face Enrichment Sessions Virtual & In-Person Faculty Support Global Opportunities South Korea Conditional Work Holiday & University Study Thailand University Pathways & Work while Studying PROGRAM SCHEDULE Academic Timeline Grade 11 (SY 2025 - 2026) Fast-Tracked: Jan 2026 to Jul 2026 | Modules 1 & 2 Grade 12 (SY 2026 - 2027) Regular Program: Aug 2026 to Mar 2027 | Modules 3 & 4 Why Enroll at NCIP - IIIP? Education at your doorstep 48 NCIP Learning Centers nationwide 100% online + face-to-face enrichment Dedicated teacher-facilitators Internationally recognized ISO 17024 certificates Clear pathways to global work & study STEP BY STEP NCIP “Snap & Submit” Enrollment Paradigm Target Audience: Grade 11 & Grade 12 Students | Timeline: January Enrollment PHASE 1: DISTRIBUTION Community Hubs: Physical forms distributed to Barangay halls, Tribal centers, and local partner schools. Digital Copy: Printable PDF pinned in GC and Facebook page for those with printers. PHASE 2: SNAP & SUBMIT Fill Out: Student completes physical form. Snap: Take a clear photo of the form. Upload: Join GC and upload photo with: Last Name, First Name, Middle Name, Birthday, [LRN if available], Grade Level. PHASE 3: ENCODING & VERIFICATION The Encoders: Staff monitor GC. Data Entry: Details manually encoded into student database. Validation: Staff ensure legibility and completeness. PHASE 4: OFFICIAL ONBOARDING Generation: COE & LMS credentials created. Distribution: Admin sends PM in GC with digital COE and credentials. Welcome Guide: Infographic explains login instructions. View Enrollment Form ↗ CURRICULUM HUMSS View full curriculum ↗ DIGITAL SKILLS Competency-Based Curriculum (CBC) Modules Hands-on training programs designed to prepare learners for global careers. Cyber Security The Cyber Security Competency-Based Curriculum is a comprehensive face-to-face training program designed to equip learners with essential to advanced skills in protecting digital systems, networks, and information assets. It follows a structured progression from basic workplace competencies to common, core, applied, and advanced cybersecurity competencies, covering areas such as: Cyber risk assessment Security governance Network and endpoint security Cloud security, threat intelligence Malware analysis, digital forensics Incident response, disaster recovery Business continuity Duration: 405 hours. Emphasizes hands-on learning through simulations, labs, and real-world scenarios. Prepares trainees for professional roles and certifications while promoting ethical practices, safety, collaboration, and innovation. Smart City The Smart City Competency-Based Curriculum is a structured face-to-face program designed to develop essential skills and knowledge for planning, managing, and implementing smart city solutions. It covers basic, common, core, applied, and advanced competencies, progressing from workplace communication, teamwork, safety, and innovation to specialized areas such as: Smart infrastructure IoT for urban connectivity Smart grids, intelligent transport systems E-governance, data ethics, public-private partnerships Big data analytics, artificial intelligence Real-time urban monitoring, citizen engagement Duration: 405 hours. Emphasizes sustainability, climate resilience, green technologies, and community participation. Combines theory with practical applications for ICT-driven urban development. Supply Chain The Supply Chain Management Competency-Based Curriculum is a structured face-to-face program designed to equip learners with essential skills for managing the flow of goods, information, and services. It covers basic, common, core, applied, and advanced competencies, starting with workplace communication, teamwork, safety, environmental standards, and innovation, progressing to specialized areas such as: Supplier evaluation, strategic sourcing, contract negotiation Sustainable procurement Transportation and distribution, warehouse management, inventory control Logistics automation, demand forecasting Sales and operations planning, predictive analytics, risk management Regulatory compliance, quality assurance, supply chain resilience Duration: 405 hours. Emphasizes practical application through case studies, simulations, and hands-on activities, preparing learners for efficient, sustainable, and resilient supply chain systems. Digital Engineering The Digital Engineering Competency-Based Curriculum is designed to equip learners with essential skills and knowledge in applying digital technologies across the engineering lifecycle. It integrates basic, common, core, applied, and advanced competencies, covering areas such as: Digital design and modeling Automation and smart systems Data analytics in engineering Simulation, prototyping, and testing Software and hardware integration Duration: 405 hours. Focuses on practical, hands-on experience to prepare learners for modern engineering roles in global industries. Note: CBC Release Upon Request TAKE YOUR NEXT STEP Empowering Indigenous Futures Globally ENROLL NOW! ↗ Explore Regular SHS ↗"
