        "title": "Search results",
        "text": "About National Literacy SRIC Awards and Recognition nla.html Search results National Literacy Award Address Quick Links Gallery Contact Us Visit Us National Literacy Award SRIC AWARDS AND RECOGNITION 2nd Place · Gawad Liyab 2024 · National Recognition ← → St. Robert's International College has earned national recognition by securing 2nd place in the 2024 Gawad Liyab – National Literacy Award. The institution was acknowledged for its outstanding and innovative implementation of multidisciplinary programs in arts, culture, and technology, collectively known as IMPACT.This national recognition underscores the institution’s significant role in advancing literacy, education, and community development through creative and transformative approaches. The IMPACT initiative reflects a progressive model of integrating multiple disciplines that are responsive to both local and global needs. By emphasizing the interconnectedness of arts, culture, and technology, St. Robert’s International College continues to demonstrate how education can be a powerful tool in shaping inclusive, sustainable communities.The National Literacy Award, conferred through the Gawad Liyab program, is one of the country’s most esteemed platforms that honors institutions and local government units (LGUs) making meaningful contributions to the promotion of functional literacy. Being chosen as a national awardee highlights the institution's systematic, community-driven, and results-based programs that empower individuals, especially in underserved sectors.The achievement affirms the institution’s long-standing dedication to academic excellence, cultural enrichment, technological advancement, and community service. As initiatives like IMPACT continue to grow and evolve, they will remain instrumental in equipping learners with the knowledge, skills, and values necessary for active citizenship and nation-building.Looking ahead, this milestone sets a strong foundation for further collaboration between educational institutions and local government partners, with the shared goal of creating an informed, empowered, and literate society."
